.TH MIXRAND 1 "2026" "mixrand 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mixrand \- secure random byte generator with multi-source entropy mixing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mixrand
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B mixrand
\fIdaemon\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B mixrand
\fIcheck\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B mixrand
\fIbench\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B mixrand
\fIlist-sources\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B mixrand
\fIcompletions\fR \fISHELL\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mixrand
generates secure random bytes by cryptographically mixing multiple
independent entropy sources \(em hardware RNGs, CPU instructions
(RDRAND/RDSEED/RNDR), the Linux kernel pool, and optional HSM or
secure\-element sources. Inputs are combined via BLAKE2b\-256 (or HKDF)
with domain separation and length\-prefixed framing, seeded into a
ChaCha20 CSPRNG. NIST SP 800\-90B continuous health tests (Repetition
Count + Adaptive Proportion) reject stuck or biased sources before they
reach the mixer.
.SH OPTIONS (GENERATE MODE)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-bytes\fR \fIN\fR
Number of random bytes to generate. Default 32, maximum 100 MiB.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFMT\fR
Output format: \fBhex\fR (default), \fBhex\-upper\fR, \fBraw\fR,
\fBbase64\fR, \fBbase64url\fR, \fBuuencode\fR, \fBtext\fR, \fBoctal\fR,
\fBbinary\fR.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR
Write output to \fIPATH\fR instead of stdout.
.TP
\fB\-\-count\fR \fIN\fR
Generate \fIN\fR independent outputs (up to 10000).
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Debug\-level logging.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Error\-level logging only (mutually exclusive with
.BR \-v ).
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-config\fR
Print the effective configuration as TOML and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR
Configuration file path (default
.IR /etc/mixrand.toml ).
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR \fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version \-\-verbose\fR
Print extended build provenance (git commit, UTC build timestamp,
.BR rustc (1)
version, target triple, enabled Cargo features) and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMAND: daemon
Linux\-only. Monitors
.I /proc/sys/kernel/random/entropy_avail
and injects mixed entropy via
.BR ioctl (2)
.B RNDADDENTROPY
when it falls below \fB\-\-threshold\fR.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-threshold\fR \fIBITS\fR
Entropy bits threshold below which to inject (default 256).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interval\fR \fISECS\fR
Poll interval in seconds (default 5).
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-batch\-size\fR \fIBYTES\fR
Bytes to inject per round (default 64).
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-credit\-ratio\fR \fIBITS\fR
Bits of entropy credited per byte, 1\(en8 (default 4).
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fINAME\fR
Drop privileges to this user after opening
.IR /dev/random .
.TP
\fB\-\-pid\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR
Write PID to \fIPATH\fR; detects stale PID files on startup and uses
\fBO_CREAT|O_EXCL\fR to prevent two daemons from racing the same file.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-self\-test\fR
Skip the startup self\-test (debug only). By default the daemon probes
every built source and runs NIST SP 800\-90B health tests on a 256\-byte
sample before signalling systemd
.BR READY=1 ;
if every source fails, the daemon exits non\-zero instead of entering
the main loop.
.SH SIGNALS
The daemon installs handlers for:
.TP
.B SIGTERM, SIGINT
Graceful shutdown. The PID file is removed before the daemon exits.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload
.I /etc/mixrand.toml
(or the path passed to
.BR \-\-config ).
Does not reopen
.IR /dev/random ,
re\-probe source plugins, or re\-run the startup self\-test \(em
restart the service for those.
.SH SUBCOMMAND: check
Run FIPS 140\-2 statistical tests and entropy estimates against each
entropy source.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-duration\fR \fISPEC\fR
Duration (e.g.
.BR 30s ", " 5m ", " 1h ", " 2d ";
bare number = minutes). Default 1m.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-sample\-size\fR \fIBYTES\fR
Bytes per sample (FIPS tests need >=2500). Default 2500.
.TP
\fB\-\-sources\fR \fINAME,NAME,...\fR
Limit to the listed sources (comma\-separated, case\-insensitive).
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fIFMT\fR
Output format: \fBtext\fR (default), \fBjson\fR, \fBcsv\fR.
.SH SUBCOMMAND: bench
Measure per\-source throughput (bytes/s, samples/s) over a fixed
duration. Unlike
.BR check ,
does not run statistical tests.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-duration\fR \fISPEC\fR
Per\-source benchmark duration (default 3s).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-sample\-size\fR \fIBYTES\fR
Bytes per
.BR collect (3)
call (default 4096).
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-bytes\fR \fIN\fR
Stop a source once it has produced \fIN\fR bytes, even if the
duration budget remains.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fIFMT\fR
Output format: \fBtext\fR (default), \fBjson\fR, \fBcsv\fR.
.SH SUBCOMMAND: list-sources
Probe every configured entropy source and print its availability, type,
and description.
.SH SUBCOMMAND: completions
Emit shell completion scripts.
.I SHELL
is one of
.BR bash ", " zsh ", " fish ", " elvish ", " powershell .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Configuration layers merge in the order:
defaults \(-> /etc/mixrand.toml (or \-\-config) \(-> MIXRAND_* env vars
\(-> CLI flags. Later layers override earlier ones.
.PP
Common environment variables:
.TP
.B MIXRAND_ENABLE_RDSEED
true|false \(em toggle RDSEED instruction.
.TP
.B MIXRAND_PREFER
rdseed|rdrand|xstore|rndr|rndrrs.
.TP
.B MIXRAND_MIXER_MODE
blake2b|hkdf.
.TP
.B MIXRAND_TPM2_TCTI
TCTI string for TPM 2.0 (e.g. device:/dev/tpmrm0).
.TP
.B MIXRAND_PKCS11_PIN
PKCS#11 user PIN \(em always prefer this over
.BR \-\-pkcs11\-pin .
.TP
.B MIXRAND_YUBIHSM_PASSWORD
YubiHSM authentication password \(em always prefer this over
.BR \-\-yubihsm\-password .
.PP
See the full list in
.IR docs/config.example.toml .
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate 32 random hex bytes:
.PP
.RS
.B mixrand
.RE
.PP
Generate a printable 24\-character password:
.PP
.RS
.B "mixrand -n 24 -f text"
.RE
.PP
Dump 1 MiB of raw random bytes to a file:
.PP
.RS
.B "mixrand -n 1048576 -f raw -o /tmp/keydata.bin"
.RE
.PP
Run statistical tests for 30 seconds and emit JSON:
.PP
.RS
.B "mixrand check -d 30s --output-format json"
.RE
.PP
Benchmark throughput of every source:
.PP
.RS
.B "mixrand bench -d 5s --output-format csv"
.RE
.PP
Run as an entropy daemon on Linux, dropping to an unprivileged user:
.PP
.RS
.B "mixrand daemon --user _entropy --pid-file /run/mixrand.pid"
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Entropy collection failed, I/O error, or runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
No entropy sources are available or every source failed the startup
self\-test.
.TP
.B 64
Invalid argument or unknown flag (maps to sysexits(3)
.BR EX_USAGE ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mixrand.toml
Default configuration file path (optional).
.TP
.I /dev/hwrng
Hardware RNG character device (Linux).
.TP
.I /dev/random
Kernel blocking entropy pool (Linux; daemon mode writes here).
.TP
.I /run/mixrand/mixrand.pid
Default PID file for the daemon when used with the shipped systemd unit.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/mixrand.service
Shipped systemd unit; see
.IR deploy/systemd/mixrand.service
in the source tree.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/mixrand.conf
Creates the runtime directory on boot; see
.IR deploy/systemd/mixrand.tmpfiles.d.conf .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getrandom (2),
.BR random (4),
.BR haveged (8),
.BR tpm2_getrandom (1).
.SH STANDARDS
NIST SP 800\-90B (continuous health tests), FIPS 140\-2 (statistical
tests), RFC 5869 (HKDF-style mixer), RFC 7539 (ChaCha20 CSPRNG).
